e the government  just simply refuses to negotiate though  at all until the barricades that have  effectively cut off the favelas from the  outside world are removed and they won't  remove them  so we are at a complete impasse and  every single day people are dying  in conflict between the police and the  ordinary people  and in the background drug gangs are  moving in at the same time  absolutely everyone says that's  happening because there's no law and  order here now  the clashes have been remarkably violent  and the police have been condemned by  many for their heavy-handed tactics  against the demonstrators  they accept some of the criticism but  say they're being fired at and intend to  smash the gangs  this is their video  nope  despite appearances there is an  overwhelming tension on the barricaded  streets now close to traffic  inside mass men play with little  children  is this a revolutionary leader or a  gangster grooming new recruits  in this febrile chaos he might well be  both  stuart ramsey sky news cali colombia
 

